  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-cf-minimus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Acestrorhynchus minimus is a barracuda tetra from Amazonia. Unlike most predatory fishes, it stays small, growing to only about 8-10 cm in length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-cf-minimus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Unfortunately the species is imported only very rarely.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-cf-minimus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Barracuda tetras are widely distributed in South America with 14 currently recognized species. From scientific collections A. minimus is known from Brazil, Venezuela and the Brazilian-Colombian border area. Its type locality is the Lago Jacaré at the Rio Trombetas in Brazil. The specimens illustrated on the page are from Peru, but all diagnostic characteristics of the species fit.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-cf-minimus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Most barracuda tetra species grow to 20-30 cm and need very large aquariums. A. minimus grows to only about 8-10 cm and can be accommodated excellently in medium-sized aquariums of perhaps 120 cm edge length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-cf-minimus-2/",
      "html": "<p>From morphologically similar, large-bodied species, A. minimus can be most reliably distinguished by the fact that it has only a dark spot on the root of the tail, but not at the end of the gill cover.</p>"
    }
  ],
